WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.205
Feedback is the foundation of performance improvement.

00:00:03.205 --> 00:00:03.995
Without feedback,

00:00:03.995 --> 00:00:07.190
performers may repeat the same approach and mistake familiarity for effectiveness.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:11.000
Useful feedback connects actions, decisions, outcomes, and context.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
It helps the performer understand what worked, what did not,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.000
and what needs to change before the next attempt.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.955
Measurement should include more than final outcomes.

00:00:17.955 --> 00:00:22.000
Outcome measures matter, but they can hide whether the process was sound or merely lucky.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Process measures, quality measures, decision records, peer review,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.935
and after-action reviews help show how the result was produced.

00:00:27.935 --> 00:00:31.000
They make it easier to improve the reasoning and behavior behind the outcome,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
not just celebrate or criticize the end state.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Calibration means matching confidence to actual performance, accuracy, or likelihood.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Poor calibration can show up as overconfidence, where certainty exceeds evidence,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.955
or underconfidence, where useful skill is not trusted enough to act.

00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:49.000
Calibration improves when performers compare expectations with results,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.900
review decisions honestly, and learn which cues are reliable under which conditions.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.210
The challenge is to measure what matters without turning performance into shallow

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.000
score-chasing.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.900
Vanity metrics can create activity without capability.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.000
A strong measurement system asks whether the measure reflects real quality,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.955
whether it encourages the desired behavior, and whether it helps people improve.

00:01:06.955 --> 00:01:09.230
The purpose of measurement is learning and reliability,

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.000
not a scoreboard that rewards shortcuts.
